WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Canva just build its own ai image maker that plans designs before it draws them, and you can try it right now. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 205. From there we hit a deep dive on designer style planning, an agent that taps a real iPhone, a physio experiment, and quick bits. The design platform Canva just released its first in-house image model, called Canva Craft, ProPakistani Reports. In-house just means Canva built this one itself, instead of barred

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.520
someone else's picture maker. Millions of students and creators already use

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:39.060
Canva for posters and social graphics, so this lands right where people already

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:44.360
work. Most image AI's jump straight to colored pixels like dumping paint on a

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.380
canvas and hoping the poster looks organized. Crafts starts with a layout pass that

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:54.740
decides where objects sit, how big they should be, and where text belongs. That two

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:59.200
step approach keeps each piece separate, instead of baking everything into one flat

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.800
picture. Think of stickers on a locker versus one painted mural. You can peel one sticker

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.480
without wrecking the rest. If you have ever tried to move one object in an AI picture

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:15.100
and watch the whole thing fall apart, that change feels huge. The model supports resolutions

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:21.200
up to 2k, which is a sharp, high detail picture, and more than 30 different aspect ratios.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:27.860
Aspect ratio is just the shape of the frame, like square versus wide, so the same description can

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.780
become a square Instagram post or a wide desktop wallpaper without extra work.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.980
Canva trained craft on thousands of human-created designs from its own template library, instead

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.580
of relying mainly on photographs.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.500
That library includes posters, social media graphics, presentations, infographics, menus,

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.620
and layouts packed with lettering.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.900
The model is learning how text, pictures, and other pieces should be arranged.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.940
The way a yearbook staff learns from old yearbooks.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:02.280
Because those templates already follow real design rules, the output tends to place readable

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.220
text correctly.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.080
It also tends to keep objects from overlapping in awkward ways.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.820
If you make YouTube thumbnails, TikTok graphics, or school presentations, you can generate

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:16.760
a picture and then tweak just the text or one character without starting over.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:23.420
Craft also connects to Canva Magic, the company's existing image to design tool, so a generated

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.700
created picture can become editable layers inside the same project.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.340
Layers are like separate sheets of clear plastic stacked together.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.300
You can move the title sheet without smearing the background.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:39.440
Canva is already building two faster versions called craft fast and craft ultra fast, aimed

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.980
at lowering generation costs and speeding up results.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.560
Craft runs inside Canva's free dream lab section, so you do not need a separate app.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:53.400
Canva plans to let other AI assistants, such as chat GPT and Google's Gemini, call

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.180
craft through something called model context protocol.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:02.600
Model context protocol, or MCP, is a shared handshake that lets different AI tools pass

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:03.620
jobs to each other.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.940
That would let you ask those chat bots for a canvas style graphic, and then open it directly

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.420
in Canva for more editing.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.400
You can try this on the Canva website right now.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:19.140
Now, open any design, click the Dream Lab button, and type a prompt like, a colorful poster

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.180
for a school science fair with big readable title at the top.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.180
Watch the planning step happen before the picture appears, then drag the layers around

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.560
like normal canva pieces.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.240
You know that school poster moment when you refuse to color until the title has a home.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:38.530
You decide where the heading goes, how big the picture should be, and which colors will

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.490
actually stand out.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.850
Craft works in two clear steps that match that habit.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:47.890
First, it reads your words and builds an invisible blueprint. That blueprint lists

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:53.370
every object, its size, its position, and even where the wording should sit, like a seating

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:58.290
chart for a group project. Only after that plan is finished does the second step turn the

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:03.730
blueprint into actual colored pixels. Because the plan exists on its own, the system can

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:08.790
catch problems early, such as text covering an important object, instead of guessing the

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:13.690
whole poster at once. Picture freehand drawing versus putting a ruler and light guidelines

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:18.650
down first. The guidelines do not show in the final art, but they keep the letters straight.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:23.770
Training on real canvas templates helps that blueprint follow the same spacing and hierarchy

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:29.270
rules human designers already use. Hierarchy here just means what should shout and what should

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:35.230
whisper, like a huge title and a smaller date. Each plan piece stays on its own layer afterward,

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:39.730
so you can drag one element later without the rest of the picture shifting or breaking.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:45.050
Once you have seen that two-step habit, the designer brain talk stops sounding mystical.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.710
It is layout first, crayon second.

00:04:48.775 --> 00:04:53.955
A developer built a free tool shared on Reddit that lets any AI agent see your iPhone screen

00:04:53.955 --> 00:04:55.895
and press buttons on the actual device.

00:04:56.475 --> 00:04:59.135
No simulator and no extra app sitting on the phone.

00:04:59.775 --> 00:05:01.955
The real glass in your hand is what gets tapped.

00:05:01.955 --> 00:05:07.775
The Mac connects over Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, then the AI gets a fresh screenshot after every

00:05:07.775 --> 00:05:09.555
tap so it can react like a person.

00:05:10.155 --> 00:05:14.955
Fresh screenshots after every tap are like checking the chessboard after each move, instead

00:05:14.955 --> 00:05:16.875
of playing the whole game with your eyes closed.

00:05:17.455 --> 00:05:22.695
The iPhone shares its screen from Safari over local Wi-Fi, and the Mac acts as a Bluetooth

00:05:22.695 --> 00:05:23.755
keyboard and mouse.

00:05:24.375 --> 00:05:29.435
That gives the agent's screenshot and input tools through MCP, the same kind of handshake

00:05:29.435 --> 00:05:30.615
we mentioned with Canva.

00:05:30.615 --> 00:05:36.095
The agent can open Instagram, scroll, watch a reel, and like a post all on your physical

00:05:36.095 --> 00:05:36.515
phone.

00:05:36.975 --> 00:05:40.995
It is a bit like handing a careful sibling the remote while they watch the TV after

00:05:40.995 --> 00:05:43.635
every button, except the sibling is software.

00:05:44.235 --> 00:05:49.575
The tool works with any AI agent that has strong computer-use skills, including chat GPT

00:05:49.575 --> 00:05:50.395
and codex.

00:05:50.875 --> 00:05:56.035
Computer-use skills just means the AI can look at a screen and click or type the way you would.

00:05:56.515 --> 00:05:59.495
Your existing subscription is enough with no extra cost.

00:05:59.495 --> 00:06:04.915
You only need an iPhone and an Apple Silicon Mac, which is a Mac that uses Apple's own

00:06:04.915 --> 00:06:05.515
processors.

00:06:06.115 --> 00:06:10.035
Windows and Linux versions are coming soon, along with multi-device support.

00:06:10.555 --> 00:06:15.375
Find that Reddit post, download the free release from GitHub, pair your phone, and ask

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:21.075
an AI like ChatGPT, with computer use turned on to open Instagram and like the first real.

00:06:21.675 --> 00:06:23.495
Then just watch what happens on your screen.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:28.530
ChatGPT built one person a physio plan that they say actually worked.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:33.850
The user had months of back and shoulder pain, described the symptoms, and got a step-by-step

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:34.690
rehab routine.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.650
Rest alone had not helped.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:41.310
Following the exercises for two months led to full recovery without paying for sessions.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:46.670
The routine included clear progressions, meaning the moves get a little harder over time.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:51.070
Plus rest days like a coach's practice calendar instead of just stretch forever.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.890
You can try a curiosity version safely.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:59.330
Open chat GPT and type, I have lower back pain that gets worse after sitting all day.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:03.750
Give me a beginner-friendly daily routine with clear progressions and rest days.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.530
Follow it if you want and track how you feel.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.230
This is just for curiosity.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.750
See a real doctor for anything serious.

00:07:11.861 --> 00:07:17.261
People are using new AI tools to run classic games like Wind Waker on iPhones or Halo inside

00:07:17.261 --> 00:07:20.201
web browsers, and the projects are spreading fast.

00:07:20.201 --> 00:07:25.521
Over the past month, these unexpected ports have shown up again and again, thanks to the

00:07:25.521 --> 00:07:31.561
latest AI decomplation and recompilation tools. Those tools help unpack old game code

00:07:31.561 --> 00:07:36.241
and rebuild it so new devices can run it, a bit like taking a worn cassette and making

00:07:36.241 --> 00:07:41.481
a phone play the songs. It shows how AI is lowering the barrier to experimenting with old

00:07:41.481 --> 00:07:47.448
favorites in brand new ways, according to the Verge. Starting Monday, government computers

00:07:47.448 --> 00:07:52.028
and Sweden will block chat GPT and clawed for staff over security concerns.

00:07:52.568 --> 00:07:54.768
Clawed is another popular AI chatbot.

00:07:55.288 --> 00:08:00.288
The decision affects staff machines in the government offices, where sensitive official information

00:08:00.288 --> 00:08:01.208
might be involved.

